.TH DIALSPEECH 2
.SH NAME
dialspeech \- what was said to a telephone, as a number to dial
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "dialspeech.m";
dialspeech := load Dialspeech Dialspeech->PATH;
Said: import dialspeech;

Said: adt {
	what:	int;	# Nothing, Number or Name
	call:	int;	# began with call, dial, phone or ring
	number:	string;
	name:	string;
	kind:	string;	# mobile, work, home, main; nil for any
};

init:	fn();
parse:	fn(text: string): ref Said;
lookup:	fn(contacts, name, kind: string): (string, string, string, string);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Dialspeech
reads speech recognised (as
.IR speech9p 's
.B hear
gives it) as a phone's voice dialling reads it.
.PP
.I Parse
reads
.IR text .
A leading
.BR call ,
.BR dial ,
.B phone
or
.B ring
sets
.BR call .
Words that are all a number's make a
.BR Number :
digits said
.RB ( zero
to
.BR nine ,
.B oh
for 0), teens and tens
.RB ( "nine eleven"
is 911,
.B "twenty five"
25),
.B double
and
.B triple
before a digit,
.B hundred
after one and
.B thousand
after any,
.B star
or
.B asterisk
for
.BR * ,
.B pound
or
.B hash
for
.BR # ,
and
.B plus
first only, for
.BR + ;
and numbers written as numbers,
.BR 555-1234 ,
.BR "(555) 123-4567" ,
.BR "+1 555 123 4567" .
Anything else is a
.BR Name ,
in lower case, without the words around it that are not part of it
.RB ( please ,
.BR at ,
.BR on ,
.BR her ,
.BR the ...)
and with the kind of number said taken out of it:
.B mobile
(or
.BR cell ),
.B work
(or
.BR office ),
.B home
or
.BR main ,
so
.B "call Sarah at work"
is the name
.B sarah
and the kind
.BR work .
.PP
.I Lookup
finds a name in an address book,
.I contacts
in
.BR /phone/contacts 's
form: a line
.IB name \et kind \et number
each, lines beginning
.B #
ignored.
A contact whose whole name was said is taken before one with a word of
it, and that before one with it inside a word.
It returns the number, the contact's name and the number's kind as the
book has them, and nil; or nil and why not: no such name, two people
answer to it (both named, so the caller can ask which), or no number of
the kind asked for.
With no kind asked, a mobile number is taken first.
